# drive.config — per-feature config for drive.sh. Copy to drive.config and edit.
# Sourced by bash, so: VAR=value, no spaces around '='.
#
# LAYERING: the global defaults file (~/.config/pipeline-driver/drive.defaults, see
# drive.defaults.example) is sourced BEFORE this file and carries every stable
# cross-feature preference (transport, model/gateway, tuning, YOLO, …). This file
# holds ONLY the per-feature facts — anything set here overrides the defaults for
# this feature, so keep it to the three lines below (plus the per-run handle).
# Without a defaults file, drive.sh's built-in defaults apply (claude transport,
# IMPL_MODEL=haiku, standard tuning) — the three lines still suffice.

# The local clone of the TARGET repo (the git+md state bus). The driver only ever
# reads origin/<BRANCH> refs from here; the driven impl child shares this checkout.
WORKDIR=/path/to/your/target-repo

# Trunk branch (where .pipeline metadata + the frozen spec live). Often main/master.
BRANCH=main

# The .pipeline/<feature> directory name.
FEATURE=my-feature

# Orca transport only: pin the impl terminal PER RUN — handles are runtime-issued
# and die on app restart; titles are unreliable (field-tested: the coder TUI renamed
# its own tab mid-setup). Get it from `orca terminal list --json` right before the run.
# ORCA_TERMINAL_HANDLE=term_...

# Rare per-feature overrides: ANY variable documented in drive.defaults.example may
# be set here to override it for THIS feature only (e.g. IMPL_MODEL=sonnet for a
# hairier codebase). Do NOT bulk-copy stable values here — that defeats the layering.
